    "title": "Bulldogs' baseball team holding 13-gun raffle to support upcoming season - NewsBreak",
    "text": "15 hours ago Danny Federico editor@riverbendnews.org The Suwannee High School baseball program is holding a 13-gun raffle as a fundraiser for its upcoming season. One firearm will be raffled off during every home baseball game from February through April. The raffle includes the following guns: Shotguns: A Mossberg Semi-Automatic Turkey .410 gauge. A Winchester Marine 12 gauge. An ATI Roadagent 12 gauge. A Retay Gordion Max7 (3 inch) 12 gauge. Pistols: A Colt Cobra .38 Special. A stainless steel Smith & Wesson 686 (6-inch barrel) .357. An FN509 MT 9 millimeter. A Sig Sauer P365 Macro 9 millimeter. Rifles: A Henry Golden Boy .22LR. A Howa M1500 Sup. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
